# Agent Rules — Competitor Research Project

These rules apply to everything the agent does in this project, every run.

## Before Starting Any Research
- Always read context.md and rubric.md before doing anything else.
- If context.md is empty or missing key sections, ask the user the setup
  questions conversationally in chat (see .cursor/commands/research.md,
  Step 1) before proceeding. Do not guess or invent product context.
- If rubric.md is empty, use its defaults. Never invent scoring criteria
  that aren't in rubric.md.

## Competitor Discovery
- Search for competitors based on context.md's product category. Do not
  ask the user to approve the list before proceeding — just post it as
  a visible update in chat.
- If the user previously excluded a competitor (noted in context.md),
  never include it again without being asked.

## Flow Capture
- If a competitor blocks access (login wall, CAPTCHA, paywall), skip it,
  mark it "not captured" in the final report, and continue with the rest.
  Never stop the entire run because one competitor is blocked.
- Never fabricate screenshots, scores, or findings for a competitor that
  couldn't be captured. Missing data stays missing and visible as such.
- Screenshot naming convention:
  research/[flow]-[date]/[competitor]/step-01-[short-label].png
  (zero-padded step numbers, lowercase, hyphens not spaces)

## Progress Updates
- Post a short update after each competitor is captured, not after each
  individual screenshot. Example: "Captured Notion ✅, Linear ✅, Asana ⚠️ (blocked by login)"
- Do not narrate every tool call in detail — the task list / progress
  line is enough. Keep the chat readable.

## Scoring
- Every score must include a one-line reason. A number with no reason
  is not acceptable output.
- Score consistently against the definitions in rubric.md — do not
  improvise what a "4" means if the rubric already defines it.

## Output
- Build both the local HTML report and the Paper report as primary
  outputs, per output-template.md. If Paper MCP fails or isn't
  connected, still produce the HTML report in full — never skip output
  entirely because one destination failed.
- Follow output-template.md's structure exactly, every run, so reports
  stay comparable over time.

## Memory
- Before building the final report, check Memory for a prior run of the
  same flow. If one exists, add a "What Changed Since Last Run" section
  as described in output-template.md.
- After finishing, save this run's patterns and scores to Memory for
  future comparison.

## General
- When uncertain whether to ask the user or proceed, prefer asking only
  at the two checkpoints defined in research.md (competitor list, scope).
  Do not ask for approval at every step — that defeats the point of
  automation.
- Never commit credentials, API keys, or .env contents to any file this
  agent writes.
